<details class="detail-card admin-tips">
  <summary class="detail-card-heading">Maintenance tips &amp; scripts</summary>

  <p class="course-address">All commands run in Render: <strong>junior-golf-wales &rarr; Shell</strong>. A script must be committed and deployed before the Shell can see it.</p>

  <h3>Find new junior events (BRS opens scan)</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Scans every page of the BRS Golf open competitions listing for Wales and queues junior events into <a href="/admin/submissions">Submissions</a> for review. Nothing is published automatically. Already-queued and already-listed events are skipped, so it's safe to re-run. Worth doing monthly from February to August, when clubs publish their opens.</p>
  <pre><code>node scripts/scan-brs-opens.js --all    # check the parser: prints every competition read
node scripts/scan-brs-opens.js          # dry run: junior matches only
node scripts/scan-brs-opens.js --save   # queue matches for review</code></pre>
  <p class="scorecard-note">If <code>--all</code> shows 0 results or garbled lines, BRS has changed their page layout and the parser needs updating.</p>

  <h3>Course scorecards</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Scorecards belong to the <strong>club</strong>: open <a href="/admin/clubs">Clubs</a>, edit the club, and use <strong>Import scorecard from a photo &rarr;</strong> in the Course scorecard section. Every event at that club uses it automatically, and it shows on the club page. Par and yardage are worked out from the card. Approved clubs can also manage their own card from the club portal.</p>
  <p class="course-address">Only override on an event (tick <em>Override the scorecard for this event only</em>) when it plays a different course or layout, such as a short course or another course at a multi-course venue. Different tees on the same card just need the junior tees note. Photo import needs <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code> set in Render &rarr; Environment.</p>

  <h3>Fill in club details automatically</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Researches clubs with missing details (address, website, email, social links, logo, par, yardage, description and scorecard where published) and queues them in <a href="/admin/club-suggestions">Club suggestions</a>. Each value shows its source; tick the ones to accept. Needs <code>ANTHROPIC_API_KEY</code>, with web search enabled for your organisation in the Anthropic Console. Costs roughly 10-20p per club.</p>
  <pre><code>node scripts/add-south-wales-clubs.js            # one-off: add the 79 South Wales clubs
node scripts/enrich-clubs.js --dry-run --limit 2 # try it, queue nothing
node scripts/enrich-clubs.js --limit 10          # research the next 10 clubs with gaps
node scripts/enrich-clubs.js --club radyr-golf-club   # one club (add --redo to repeat)</code></pre>

  <h3>Find clubs' open competitions and junior pages</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Crawls each club's website for its open competitions page (including its BRS opens listing) and its junior golf page, and queues them in <a href="/admin/club-suggestions">Club suggestions</a>. No AI cost. Worth re-running each spring when clubs publish new opens.</p>
  <pre><code>node scripts/find-club-links.js --dry-run --limit 5
node scripts/find-club-links.js</code></pre>

  <h3>Weekly check of clubs' opens and junior pages</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Every Monday a scheduled job checks each club's open competitions and junior page and lists anything new in <a href="/admin/page-changes">Page changes</a>, then runs the BRS opens scan. To run it by hand:</p>
  <pre><code>node scripts/watch-club-pages.js --dry-run
node scripts/watch-club-pages.js</code></pre>

  <h3>Post an update on an event</h3>
  <pre><code>node scripts/add-update.js &lt;event-slug&gt; "Message"</code></pre>

  <h3>Series and event loaders</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Re-runnable; edit the data in the script, commit, then run.</p>
  <pre><code>node scripts/add-2027-junior-opens.js   # Ashburnham, Whitchurch, Abergele, Conwy
node scripts/add-junior-series.js       # Mini Masters + PING tour organisers, Mini Masters Final
node scripts/add-ping-tour-2027.js      # PING Welsh Junior Tour 2027 (Events 1 &amp; 5 still TBC)</code></pre>

  <h3>Back up the database</h3>
  <p class="course-address">From your own machine, using the External Database URL on the <strong>junior-golf-wales-db</strong> page in Render:</p>
  <pre><code>pg_dump -Fc "&lt;external-url&gt;" &gt; jgw-YYYY-MM-DD.dump</code></pre>

  <h3>Rebuild after losing the database</h3>
  <p class="course-address">Tables are created automatically on every deploy (<code>npm run migrate</code> runs as the pre-deploy step). Restore a backup with <code>pg_restore --no-owner -d "&lt;external-url&gt;" file.dump</code>, or reload from scratch in this order:</p>
  <pre><code>npm run seed
node scripts/set-club-addresses.js
node scripts/set-coordinates.js
node scripts/update-llantrisant.js
node scripts/update-radyr.js
node scripts/add-2027-junior-opens.js
node scripts/add-junior-series.js
node scripts/add-ping-tour-2027.js</code></pre>
  <p class="scorecard-note">Anything entered through the site itself (admin edits, submissions, club accounts, entry forms) only survives via a backup.</p>
</details>

